 "differences": [
  "Five of the sixteen standard deviations of the sentence-level F1/F2 changes differ from the preprint by 0.01-0.07 mel (Experiment 1 English F2 18.65 vs 18.58 and French F2 11.50 vs 11.53; Experiment 2 English F1 14.64 vs 14.57, French F1 14.53 vs 14.54 and French F2 14.13 vs 14.08); all sixteen means and the other eleven SDs match, so these are not used as checks.",
  "The checks use the preprint's numbers (PsyArXiv y6bqg, version 2); the title on the OSF project differs slightly ('Linguistic Context and the Generalization of Second Language Speech Motor Plans').",
  "Age, sex and handedness were not shared per participant in a labelled form: the files hold a 1/2 sex code whose labels are not documented, kept in participants.csv as sex_code."
 ],
